   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state finance law and the village law, in relation to coterminous municipalities",
    "basePrintNo": "S2787",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2787-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §54, St Fin L; amd §§17-1700, 17-1702, 17-1703, 17-1703-a, 17-1714 & 17-1735, Vil L",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2787\n\nTITLE  OF  BILL:   An act to amend the state finance law and the village\nlaw, in relation to coterminous municipalities\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:  To amend chapter 435 of  the  laws  of\n2012 to clarify the eligibility of certain grant programs.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection  1: Amends subparagraph (ii) of paragraph p of subdivision 10 of\nsection 54 of the State Finance Law to clarify that for purposes of  the\nCitizen  Empowerment  Tax  Credit,  when  a town and village engage in a\nco-terminus reorganization, they must choose to operate principally as a\nvillage or as a town but not both.\n\nSection 2: Amends clause 2 of subparagraph (i) of paragraph q of  subdi-\nvision  10  of  section  54 of the State Finance Law to clarify that for\npurposes of the Local Government Citizens Reorganization Grant  Program,\nwhen  a  town  and  village engage in a co-terminus reorganization, they\nmust choose to operate principally as a village or as  a  town  but  not\nboth.\n\nSection 3: Amends section 17-1700 of the Village Law to include villages\nwhich  have  annexed territory to embrace the entire territory of a town\nwithin the  purview  article  17  of  the  Village  Law  which  contains\nprovisions  that are applicable to a village embracing the entire terri-\ntory of a town.\n\nSection 4: Amends subdivision 1 of section 17-1702 of the Village Law to\nprovide that when a village annexes  territory  to  embrace  the  entire\nterritory  of  a  town  and later the borders of the village change, the\ncorresponding border of the town changes as well.\n\nSection 5: Amends subdivision 1 of section 17-1703 of the Village Law to\nprovide that when a village has been incorporated to embrace the  entire\nterritory of a town within the provisions of that section.\n\nSection  6:  Amends  subdivisions  1  and 2 of the opening paragraphs of\nsubdivisions 3 and 4 of section 17-1703 of the Village  Law  to  clarify\nthat  any  existing  coterminous  town-village  shall not be required to\nsubmit a proposition to the voters to decide if  the  coterminous  town-\nvillage shall operate principally as a town or principally as a village.\n\nSection 7: Amends subdivision 1 of section 17-1714 of the Village Law to\ninclude villages which have annexed territory to embrace the entirety of\na town within the provisions of that section.\n\nSection  8:  Amends  section  17-1735  of the Village Law to include any\nvillage which has annexed territory to embrace the entire territory of a\ntown within the provision for carrying over local town laws.\n\nSection 9: Effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  This legislation is needed to clarify that a coterminous\ntown-village  that  operates  principally  as a town or principally as a\nvillage shall be  eligible  for  the  Citizens  Empowerment  Tax  Credit\nprogram  and the Local Government Citizens Re-organization Grant program\nin order to provide consistency with the goals of these grant  programs,\nincluding  reducing  the  numbers  and  layers of local governments, and\nimproving the overall efficiency of local governments.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:  Undetermined.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
